<p>NOTES: 1997 Q4 net income was $10.9 million or $0.09 per share before timing adjustments made after discussions with the Staff of the Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>These timing adjustments include (1) moving a $25.7 million charge for information provider termination expenses out of the second quarter and recording a $24.5 million charge for that same item in the fourth quarter, and (2) restating $7.3 million in third quarter operating results.  </p>
<p>The $25.7 million charge occurred after AOL shifted from metered to flat-rate pricing in the December quarter and it decided to end certain information provider agreements and negotiated new agreements with those partners. The estimated costs associated with ending those contracts were reported at $25.7 million in the second quarter and were included in the company's restructuring charge. AOL has now moved those costs to the June quarter, based upon signed termination agreements.</p>
